<DocsLayout title="Desktop application" description="Develop and package the Tauri desktop shell for Hologram Live.">
  <h1>Desktop application</h1>
  <p>The Tauri application in <code>apps/desktop</code> packages Hologram's background service and provides a focused workspace for files and modules. Its sidebar follows the desktop navigation model and offers remembered light and dark appearances, while a system menu-bar item reports Hologram's state and provides Open, Start, Restart, Stop, and Quit actions after the main window closes.</p>

  <h2>Run in development</h2>
  <pre><code>just tauri
# equivalent to: cd apps/desktop &amp;&amp; npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code></pre>
  <p>The preparation script builds the repository's <code>hologram</code> binary and copies it to Tauri's target-specific sidecar location before the desktop shell starts.</p>

  <h2>Build a release bundle</h2>
  <pre><code>just tauri build</code></pre>
  <p>Tauri builds the web frontend, compiles the native shell, and includes the release sidecar in the platform bundle.</p>

  <h2>Command boundary</h2>
  <p>The webview can invoke these narrow application commands:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>service_start</code></li>
    <li><code>service_stop</code></li>
    <li><code>service_restart</code></li>
    <li><code>service_status</code></li>
    <li><code>modules_list</code></li>
    <li><code>history_list</code></li>
    <li><code>history_create</code></li>
    <li><code>history_get</code></li>
    <li><code>chat_send</code></li>
    <li><code>objects_list</code></li>
    <li><code>file_put</code></li>
    <li><code>object_get</code></li>
  </ul>
  <div class="note"><strong>No arbitrary shell bridge</strong>Each command maps to one fixed sidecar argument, keeping the browser-facing authority narrow.</div>
  <p><code>modules_list</code> reads Hologram's negotiated module manifest. The chat view creates and switches among durable conversation threads, then sends messages through the enabled chat module. The files view uses native open/save dialogs, uploads and renames files, lists content-addressed metadata, and downloads the stored bytes. Because the sidecar uses the normal Hologram configuration, the same surface can target a local service or a future authenticated cloud endpoint.</p>
</DocsLayout>
